import TavisRuddFiniteGeom.Papers.CubicStabilizationM1.GraphLattices.SixAxisPrimaryDiscriminantSplitting

/-!
# The six-label permutation action on the polarized source lattice

The five-axis coefficient lattice of this development is the quotient of six
labelled integral coordinates by the constant line, presented in the chart
which subtracts the sixth coordinate; its Gram matrix in that chart is
`6I₅-J₅`.  Permuting the six labels acts on that quotient, and this module
writes the action as an explicit matrix representation, extends it to the
polarized source lattice by acting trivially on the rank-two elliptic homology
factor, and derives the two intertwining identities which make the action
descend to the discriminant group of the polarization in its cokernel
presentation.

Objects and conventions.  A permutation acts on coordinate families by inverse
precomposition, so that `permutation • vector` has the value of `vector` at the
preimage label; `sixPointChartMatrix` is the matrix of the induced map in the
five-coordinate chart, over an arbitrary commutative coefficient ring.  The
alternating group of the manuscript is the one generated by the two displayed
permutations of the six labels — translation and `x ↦ -1/x` on the labelling
`0,1,2,3,4,∞` of the projective line over the field with five elements — whose
words realize, faithfully and onto, the alternating group on the five matchings
of the displayed one-factorization, by
`sixPointGeneratedAction_realizes_alternatingGroup`.  The representation built
here is defined on the whole six-label permutation group, so that alternating
action is its restriction.

Results.  The chart matrices form a monoid homomorphism from the six-label
permutation group, every one of them is an isometry of `6I₅-J₅`, and the
Kronecker extension by the identity on the elliptic homology factor is an
isometry of the source polarization.  The contragredient chart matrix, the
transpose of the matrix of the inverse permutation, intertwines the
polarization with the action and commutes with the integral cofactor in the
same sense; consequently the contragredient action descends to the discriminant
group presented as the cokernel of the polarization.  If a comparison matrix
pulling a unimodular form back to the source polarization is equivariant, in
the sense that the source action is carried to some integral action of the
target lattice, then the lattice model of the isogeny kernel and each of its
primary parts are stable under the descended action.

Trust boundary.  Every statement is about explicit integral or finite-field
matrices and finitely generated abelian groups.  No abelian scheme, elliptic
scheme, relative isogeny, Weil pairing, or geometric group action is
constructed, and the identification of these matrices and of this permutation
action with the geometric ones — in particular with the conjugation action of
the manuscript's alternating group on its six dihedral axes — is supplied
elsewhere and is not proved here.
-/

namespace TavisRuddFiniteGeom.Papers.CubicStabilizationM1

namespace GraphLattices

open scoped BigOperators
open scoped Kronecker
open scoped Matrix

section ChartRepresentation

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- The matrix, in the five-coordinate chart of the six-label quotient, of the
map induced by a permutation of the six labels.  Its entry in a row indexed by
a chart coordinate and a column indexed by a chart coordinate compares the
preimage of the row label with the column label and subtracts the same
comparison for the preimage of the omitted sixth label; the subtraction is the
passage to the quotient by the constant line. -/
def sixPointChartMatrix (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    Matrix (Fin 5) (Fin 5) R :=
  Matrix.of fun row column ↦
    (if permutation⁻¹ row.castSucc = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0) -
      (if permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6) = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0)

variable {R}

/-- Selecting a label by the chart indicators: a family vanishing at the sixth
label is recovered at every label by the corresponding indicator sum. -/
private theorem sixPointChartIndicator_sum
    (values : Fin 6 → R) (vanishing : values 5 = 0) (point : Fin 6) :
    ∑ column : Fin 5,
        (if point = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0) * values column.castSucc =
      values point := by
  fin_cases point <;>
    simp [Fin.sum_univ_succ, vanishing]

/-- The chart matrix implements inverse precomposition on difference
coordinates: applying it to the chart coordinates of a six-label family gives
the chart coordinates of the permuted family. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec_difference
    (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) (vector : Fin 6 → R) :
    sixPointChartMatrix R permutation *ᵥ
        (fun index : Fin 5 ↦ vector index.castSucc - vector 5) =
      fun index : Fin 5 ↦
        vector (permutation⁻¹ index.castSucc) - vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6)) := by
  funext row
  have vanishing : (fun point : Fin 6 ↦ vector point - vector 5) 5 = 0 := sub_self _
  have expansion :
      (sixPointChartMatrix R permutation *ᵥ
          fun index : Fin 5 ↦ vector index.castSucc - vector 5) row =
        (∑ column : Fin 5,
            (if permutation⁻¹ row.castSucc = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0) *
              (fun point : Fin 6 ↦ vector point - vector 5) column.castSucc) -
          ∑ column : Fin 5,
            (if permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6) = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0) *
              (fun point : Fin 6 ↦ vector point - vector 5) column.castSucc := by
    simp only [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, sixPointChartMatrix, Matrix.of_apply, sub_mul]
    rw [Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  rw [expansion,
    sixPointChartIndicator_sum (fun point : Fin 6 ↦ vector point - vector 5) vanishing,
    sixPointChartIndicator_sum (fun point : Fin 6 ↦ vector point - vector 5) vanishing]
  ring

/-- The six-label family with prescribed chart coordinates and vanishing sixth
coordinate. -/
def sixPointChartLift (vector : Fin 5 → R) : Fin 6 → R :=
  ![vector 0, vector 1, vector 2, vector 3, vector 4, 0]

/-- The lift has the prescribed chart coordinates. -/
theorem sixPointChartLift_difference (vector : Fin 5 → R) :
    (fun index : Fin 5 ↦
        sixPointChartLift vector index.castSucc - sixPointChartLift vector 5) = vector := by
  funext index
  fin_cases index <;> simp [sixPointChartLift]

/-- The chart matrix applied to a chart vector, computed through the lift. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec
    (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) (vector : Fin 5 → R) :
    sixPointChartMatrix R permutation *ᵥ vector =
      fun index : Fin 5 ↦
        sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ index.castSucc) -
          sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6)) := by
  conv_lhs => rw [← sixPointChartLift_difference vector]
  exact sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec_difference permutation (sixPointChartLift vector)

/-- A matrix entry read off from the bilinear pairing of standard basis
vectors. -/
private theorem matrix_entry_dotProduct {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (matrix : Matrix ι ι R) (row column : ι) :
    matrix row column = dotProduct (Pi.single row 1) (matrix *ᵥ Pi.single column 1) := by
  simp

/-- Two matrices with the same action on every vector are equal. -/
private theorem matrix_ext_of_mulVec {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    {left right : Matrix ι ι R}
    (action : ∀ vector : ι → R, left *ᵥ vector = right *ᵥ vector) :
    left = right := by
  ext row column
  have applied := congrFun (action (Pi.single column 1)) row
  simpa [Matrix.mulVec] using applied

/-- The identity permutation acts by the identity matrix. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_one :
    sixPointChartMatrix R (1 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) = 1 := by
  refine matrix_ext_of_mulVec fun vector ↦ ?_
  rw [sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec, Matrix.one_mulVec]
  funext index
  show sixPointChartLift vector index.castSucc - sixPointChartLift vector (5 : Fin 6) =
    vector index
  exact congrFun (sixPointChartLift_difference vector) index

/-- The chart matrices are multiplicative. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_mul (left right : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixPointChartMatrix R (left * right) =
      sixPointChartMatrix R left * sixPointChartMatrix R right := by
  refine (matrix_ext_of_mulVec fun vector ↦ ?_).symm
  rw [← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec right vector]
  have permuted :
      sixPointChartMatrix R left *ᵥ
          (fun index : Fin 5 ↦
            sixPointChartLift vector (right⁻¹ index.castSucc) -
              sixPointChartLift vector (right⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6))) =
        fun index : Fin 5 ↦
          sixPointChartLift vector (right⁻¹ (left⁻¹ index.castSucc)) -
            sixPointChartLift vector (right⁻¹ (left⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6))) :=
    sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec_difference left
      (fun point ↦ sixPointChartLift vector (right⁻¹ point))
  rw [permuted, sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec]
  funext index
  have inverse : ∀ point : Fin 6, (left * right)⁻¹ point = right⁻¹ (left⁻¹ point) := by
    intro point
    rw [mul_inv_rev]
    rfl
  rw [inverse, inverse]

variable (R)

/-- The permutation representation of the six labels on the five-coordinate
chart of their integral quotient by the constant line. -/
def sixPointChartRepresentation :
    Equiv.Perm (Fin 6) →* Matrix (Fin 5) (Fin 5) R where
  toFun := sixPointChartMatrix R
  map_one' := sixPointChartMatrix_one
  map_mul' := sixPointChartMatrix_mul

/-- The representation evaluates by the chart matrix. -/
theorem sixPointChartRepresentation_apply (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixPointChartRepresentation R permutation = sixPointChartMatrix R permutation :=
  rfl

variable {R}

/-- Reducing the integral chart matrix into a commutative ring gives the chart
matrix over that ring. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_map (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation).map (Int.castRingHom R) =
      sixPointChartMatrix R permutation := by
  ext row column
  show ((((if permutation⁻¹ row.castSucc = column.castSucc then (1 : ℤ) else 0) -
      (if permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6) = column.castSucc then (1 : ℤ) else 0) : ℤ)) : R) =
    (if permutation⁻¹ row.castSucc = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0) -
      (if permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6) = column.castSucc then (1 : R) else 0)
  push_cast
  by_cases rowCase : permutation⁻¹ row.castSucc = column.castSucc <;>
    by_cases lastCase : permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6) = column.castSucc <;>
      simp [rowCase, lastCase]

end ChartRepresentation

section Isometry

/-- The chart matrix acts as the descended permutation of the integral
six-label quotient. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_classFromFive (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6))
    (vector : Fin 5 → ℤ) :
    sixPointIntegralClassFromFive (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ vector) =
      sixPointIntegralQuotientPermutation permutation
        (sixPointIntegralClassFromFive vector) := by
  have difference : ∀ point : Fin 6,
      sixPointIntegralRepresentativeFromFive
          (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ vector) point -
        sixPointIntegralPermutationLinear permutation
          (sixPointIntegralRepresentativeFromFive vector) point =
        -sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6)) := by
    intro point
    have permuted := sixPointChartMatrix_mulVec (R := ℤ) permutation vector
    fin_cases point <;>
      simp [sixPointIntegralRepresentativeFromFive,
        sixPointIntegralPermutationLinear, permuted, sixPointChartLift]
  refine (Submodule.Quotient.eq _).mpr ?_
  have membership :
      (fun _ : Fin 6 ↦ -sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6))) ∈
        sixPointIntegralConstantLine := by
    rw [sixPointIntegralConstantLine, Submodule.mem_span_singleton]
    exact ⟨-sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6)), by funext _; simp⟩
  have equality :
      sixPointIntegralRepresentativeFromFive
          (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ vector) -
        sixPointIntegralPermutationLinear permutation
          (sixPointIntegralRepresentativeFromFive vector) =
        fun _ : Fin 6 ↦ -sixPointChartLift vector (permutation⁻¹ (5 : Fin 6)) := by
    funext point
    exact difference point
  rw [equality]
  exact membership

/-- Every six-label permutation acts on the five-coordinate chart by an
isometry of the coefficient form `6I₅-J₅`. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_dotProduct_gram (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6))
    (left right : Fin 5 → ℤ) :
    dotProduct (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ left)
        (sixAxisGram ℤ *ᵥ (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ right)) =
      dotProduct left (sixAxisGram ℤ *ᵥ right) := by
  rw [← sixPointIntegralDescendedPairing_classFromFive,
    ← sixPointIntegralDescendedPairing_classFromFive,
    sixPointChartMatrix_classFromFive, sixPointChartMatrix_classFromFive]
  exact sixPointIntegralDescendedPairing_permutation permutation _ _

/-- The chart matrix of every six-label permutation preserves the coefficient
matrix `6I₅-J₅`. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_gram (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation)ᵀ * sixAxisGram ℤ *
        sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation = sixAxisGram ℤ := by
  have transported : ∀ left right : Fin 5 → ℤ,
      dotProduct left
          (((sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation)ᵀ * sixAxisGram ℤ *
            sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation) *ᵥ right) =
        dotProduct (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ left)
          (sixAxisGram ℤ *ᵥ (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation *ᵥ right)) := by
    intro left right
    rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, ← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, ← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec,
      Matrix.dotProduct_mulVec, Matrix.vecMul_transpose]
  ext row column
  rw [matrix_entry_dotProduct ((sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation)ᵀ * sixAxisGram ℤ *
      sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation) row column,
    matrix_entry_dotProduct (sixAxisGram ℤ) row column, transported]
  exact sixPointChartMatrix_dotProduct_gram permutation (Pi.single row 1) (Pi.single column 1)

end Isometry

section Contragredient

/-- The contragredient chart matrix of a six-label permutation: the transpose
of the chart matrix of its inverse.  It is the matrix of the induced action on
the dual lattice written in the coordinates of the cokernel presentation of the
discriminant group. -/
def sixPointDualChartMatrix (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    Matrix (Fin 5) (Fin 5) ℤ :=
  (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹)ᵀ

/-- The chart matrices of a permutation and of its inverse are inverse. -/
theorem sixPointChartMatrix_inv_mul (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹ * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation = 1 := by
  rw [← sixPointChartMatrix_mul, inv_mul_cancel, sixPointChartMatrix_one]

/-- The contragredient chart matrix intertwines the coefficient matrix with the
chart matrix. -/
theorem sixPointDualChartMatrix_mul_gram (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation * sixAxisGram ℤ =
      sixAxisGram ℤ * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation := by
  calc sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation * sixAxisGram ℤ
      = (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹)ᵀ * sixAxisGram ℤ *
          (sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹ * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation) := by
        rw [sixPointChartMatrix_inv_mul, Matrix.mul_one]
        rfl
    _ = ((sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹)ᵀ * sixAxisGram ℤ *
          sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation⁻¹) * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, Matrix.mul_assoc, Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = sixAxisGram ℤ * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation := by
        rw [sixPointChartMatrix_gram]

/-- Cancelling a nondegenerate integral matrix on the right. -/
private theorem matrix_right_cancel {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    {left right factor : Matrix ι ι ℤ} (nondegenerate : factor.det ≠ 0)
    (equation : left * factor = right * factor) : left = right := by
  have adjugated := congrArg (fun matrix ↦ matrix * factor.adjugate) equation
  simp only [Matrix.mul_assoc, Matrix.mul_adjugate] at adjugated
  ext row column
  have entry := congrFun (congrFun adjugated row) column
  simp only [Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.mul_one, Matrix.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at entry
  exact mul_left_cancel₀ nondegenerate entry

/-- The coefficient matrix `6I₅-J₅` is nondegenerate. -/
theorem sixAxisGram_det_ne_zero : (sixAxisGram ℤ).det ≠ 0 := by
  intro vanishing
  have squared := sixAxisGram_det_sq
  rw [vanishing] at squared
  norm_num at squared

/-- The integral coefficient cofactor `I₅+J₅` intertwines the contragredient
chart matrix with the chart matrix. -/
theorem sixAxisGramCofactor_mul_dualChart (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixAxisGramCofactor * sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation =
      sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation * sixAxisGramCofactor := by
  refine matrix_right_cancel sixAxisGram_det_ne_zero ?_
  calc sixAxisGramCofactor * sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation * sixAxisGram ℤ
      = sixAxisGramCofactor * (sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation * sixAxisGram ℤ) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = sixAxisGramCofactor * (sixAxisGram ℤ * sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation) := by
        rw [sixPointDualChartMatrix_mul_gram]
    _ = (6 : ℤ) • sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation := by
        rw [← Matrix.mul_assoc, sixAxisGramCofactor_mul, Matrix.smul_mul, Matrix.one_mul]
    _ = sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation * (sixAxisGramCofactor * sixAxisGram ℤ) := by
        rw [sixAxisGramCofactor_mul, Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.mul_one]
    _ = sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation * sixAxisGramCofactor * sixAxisGram ℤ := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]

end Contragredient

section SourceLattice

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- The action of a six-label permutation on the source lattice: the chart
matrix on the axis coordinate together with the identity on the rank-two
elliptic homology coordinate. -/
def sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) R :=
  sixPointChartMatrix R permutation ⊗ₖ (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R)

variable {R}

/-- The source action moves each elliptic homology coordinate separately, by
the chart matrix on the axis coordinates. -/
theorem sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix_mulVec_apply
    (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) (vector : Fin 5 × Fin 2 → R)
    (axis : Fin 5) (spin : Fin 2) :
    (sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix R permutation *ᵥ vector) (axis, spin) =
      (sixPointChartMatrix R permutation *ᵥ fun other ↦ vector (other, spin)) axis := by
  rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fintype.sum_prod_type]
  rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl ?_
  intro otherAxis _
  have entries : ∀ otherSpin : Fin 2,
      sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix R permutation (axis, spin) (otherAxis, otherSpin) =
        sixPointChartMatrix R permutation axis otherAxis *
          (if spin = otherSpin then (1 : R) else 0) := by
    intro otherSpin
    show sixPointChartMatrix R permutation axis otherAxis *
        (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) spin otherSpin = _
    rw [Matrix.one_apply]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun otherSpin _ ↦ by rw [entries otherSpin])]
  fin_cases spin <;> simp

/-- Reducing the integral source action into a commutative ring gives the
source action over that ring. -/
theorem sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix_map (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    (sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation).map (Int.castRingHom R) =
      sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix R permutation := by
  ext row column
  obtain ⟨axis, spin⟩ := row
  obtain ⟨otherAxis, otherSpin⟩ := column
  show ((sixPointChartMatrix ℤ permutation axis otherAxis *
      (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℤ) spin otherSpin : ℤ) : R) =
    sixPointChartMatrix R permutation axis otherAxis *
      (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) spin otherSpin
  rw [Int.cast_mul]
  refine congrArg₂ (· * ·) ?_ ?_
  · have mapped := congrFun (congrFun (sixPointChartMatrix_map (R := R) permutation) axis)
      otherAxis
    exact mapped
  · rw [Matrix.one_apply, Matrix.one_apply]
    by_cases equalSpins : spin = otherSpin <;> simp [equalSpins]

/-- Every six-label permutation preserves the source polarization. -/
theorem sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix_polarization (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    (sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation)ᵀ * sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ *
        sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation = sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ := by
  rw [sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix, sixAxisSourcePolarization,
    ← Matrix.kroneckerMap_transpose, Matrix.transpose_one, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul,
    ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, sixPointChartMatrix_gram, Matrix.one_mul, Matrix.mul_one]

/-- The contragredient action of a six-label permutation on the source
lattice. -/
def sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) ℤ :=
  sixPointDualChartMatrix permutation ⊗ₖ (1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℤ)

/-- The contragredient source action intertwines the polarization with the
source action. -/
theorem sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix_mul_polarization
    (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation * sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ =
      sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ * sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation := by
  rw [sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix, sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix,
    sixAxisSourcePolarization, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul,
    sixPointDualChartMatrix_mul_gram, Matrix.one_mul, Matrix.mul_one]

/-- The integral cofactor of the source polarization intertwines the
contragredient source action with the source action. -/
theorem sixAxisSourcePolarizationCofactor_mul_dual (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixAxisSourcePolarizationCofactor * sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation =
      sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation * sixAxisSourcePolarizationCofactor := by
  rw [sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix, sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix,
    sixAxisSourcePolarizationCofactor, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul,
    sixAxisGramCofactor_mul_dualChart, Matrix.one_mul, Matrix.mul_one]

end SourceLattice

section DiscriminantAction

/-- The contragredient source action descends to the discriminant group of the
source polarization in its cokernel presentation: the polarization image of a
vector is carried to the polarization image of its transform. -/
def sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) :
    sixAxisSourceDiscriminantGroup →ₗ[ℤ] sixAxisSourceDiscriminantGroup :=
  Submodule.liftQ _
    ((latticeImage (sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ)).mkQ.comp
      (Matrix.mulVecLin (sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation)))
    (by
      intro vector membership
      obtain ⟨source, rfl⟩ := mem_latticeImage_iff.mp membership
      refine LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr ?_
      show (Submodule.Quotient.mk
        (sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation *ᵥ
          (sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ *ᵥ source)) :
            sixAxisSourceDiscriminantGroup) = 0
      rw [Matrix.mulVec_mulVec,
        sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix_mul_polarization, ← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec]
      exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).mpr
        (mem_latticeImage_iff.mpr ⟨_, rfl⟩))

/-- The descended action computes on the class of a representative. -/
theorem sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation_mk (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6))
    (vector : Fin 5 × Fin 2 → ℤ) :
    sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation permutation (Submodule.Quotient.mk vector) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk
        (sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation *ᵥ vector) :=
  rfl

section Comparison

variable {comparison target : Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) ℤ}

/-- Equivariance of a comparison matrix for one six-label permutation: the
source action of that permutation is carried by the comparison to some integral
action of the target lattice.  For a relative isogeny compatible with an action
of the manuscript's alternating group on both sides, this is the statement that
the induced comparison of integral first homology commutes with the two
actions. -/
def SixAxisComparisonEquivariant
    (comparison : Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) ℤ)
    (permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)) : Prop :=
  ∃ targetAction : Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) ℤ,
    comparison * sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation = targetAction * comparison

/-- Equivariance transports to the matrix whose columns present the lattice
model of the isogeny kernel. -/
theorem sixAxisComparisonEquivariant_transpose_target {permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)}
    (principal : target.det = 1)
    (pullback : comparisonᵀ * target * comparison = sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ)
    (equivariant : SixAxisComparisonEquivariant comparison permutation) :
    ∃ targetAction : Matrix (Fin 5 × Fin 2) (Fin 5 × Fin 2) ℤ,
      sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation * (comparisonᵀ * target) =
        comparisonᵀ * target * targetAction := by
  obtain ⟨targetAction, intertwined⟩ := equivariant
  refine ⟨targetAction, ?_⟩
  refine matrix_right_cancel
    (sixAxisPolarizationPullback_det_ne_zero principal pullback) ?_
  calc sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation * (comparisonᵀ * target) * comparison
      = sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation * (comparisonᵀ * target * comparison) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix permutation * sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ := by
        rw [pullback]
    _ = sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ * sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation := by
        rw [sixAxisSourceDualPermutationMatrix_mul_polarization]
    _ = comparisonᵀ * target * (comparison * sixAxisSourcePermutationMatrix ℤ permutation) := by
        rw [← pullback, Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = comparisonᵀ * target * (targetAction * comparison) := by rw [intertwined]
    _ = comparisonᵀ * target * targetAction * comparison := by
        simp [Matrix.mul_assoc]

/-- The lattice model of the isogeny kernel is stable under the descended
action of an equivariant comparison. -/
theorem comparisonKernelSubgroup_permutation_mem {permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)}
    (principal : target.det = 1)
    (pullback : comparisonᵀ * target * comparison = sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ)
    (equivariant : SixAxisComparisonEquivariant comparison permutation)
    {element : sixAxisSourceDiscriminantGroup}
    (member : element ∈ comparisonKernelSubgroup pullback) :
    sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation permutation element ∈
      comparisonKernelSubgroup pullback := by
  obtain ⟨targetAction, intertwined⟩ :=
    sixAxisComparisonEquivariant_transpose_target principal pullback equivariant
  obtain ⟨source, value⟩ := mem_comparisonKernelSubgroup_iff.mp member
  refine mem_comparisonKernelSubgroup_iff.mpr ⟨targetAction *ᵥ source, ?_⟩
  rw [← value, sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation_mk, Matrix.mulVec_mulVec,
    Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, intertwined]

/-- Each primary part of the lattice model of the isogeny kernel is stable
under the descended action of an equivariant comparison. -/
theorem sixAxisSourcePrimaryKernelSubgroup_permutation_mem
    {permutation : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6)} (principal : target.det = 1)
    (pullback : comparisonᵀ * target * comparison = sixAxisSourcePolarization ℤ)
    (equivariant : SixAxisComparisonEquivariant comparison permutation) (prime : ℤ)
    {element : sixAxisSourceDiscriminantGroup}
    (member : element ∈ sixAxisSourcePrimaryKernelSubgroup pullback prime) :
    sixAxisSourceDiscriminantPermutation permutation element ∈
      sixAxisSourcePrimaryKernelSubgroup pullback prime := by
  obtain ⟨kernelMember, torsionMember⟩ := Submodule.mem_inf.mp member
  refine Submodule.mem_inf.mpr
    ⟨comparisonKernelSubgroup_permutation_mem principal pullback equivariant kernelMember, ?_⟩
  refine mem_torsionBy_iff_smul_eq_zero.mpr ?_
  rw [← map_smul, mem_torsionBy_iff_smul_eq_zero.mp torsionMember, map_zero]

end Comparison

end DiscriminantAction

